lane: channel-send-fastpath
why: chunked still trails zio (175.3 vs 128.0). Measured on both
  sides now: ZStream.fromQueue averages 137.9 elements per queue
  operation, SentinelChannel 35.4. Batch size is set by how far the
  producer runs ahead, and ours cannot: sendBlocking goes through
  CanBlock.blockAccepted on EVERY element -- a slot allocated, filled
  and read -- even when the ring has room and there is nothing to wait
  for. offer() is the non-suspending send and needs none of that.
  Hypothesis to test, not assume: an offer-first fast path makes the
  producer faster, which lets the buffer accumulate, which enlarges
  the consumer's batches, which is the number that matters.
